# Code owners: a change under these paths needs an approving review from an
# owner before it merges to main (branch protection: "Require review from Code
# Owners"). They are the paths where a bug gives an engineer a wrong number
# instead of an error: the solver, the result certificates, post-processing
# (forces, envelopes, design checks), the element formulations, the design-code
# checks in the web app, and the verification documents that state what is
# proved and tested.
#
# Later lines take precedence over earlier ones. Add a team or a second owner
# here when one exists; until then the repository admin reviews.

/engine/src/solver/        @unbalancedparentheses
/engine/src/certify/       @unbalancedparentheses
/engine/src/postprocess/   @unbalancedparentheses
/engine/src/element/       @unbalancedparentheses
/web/src/lib/engine/codes/ @unbalancedparentheses
/docs/verification/        @unbalancedparentheses

# The rules themselves.
/.github/CODEOWNERS        @unbalancedparentheses
